+### Browserbase interactive sessions
+
+`@effect-agent/platform-browserbase` implements the same `InteractiveBrowser` contract on trusted
+Node and Bun hosts with Playwright 1.63 over Browserbase CDP. One enclosing Scope owns the remote
+session; application code and model Tools borrow handles from that owner. Provider credentials,
+CDP addresses, persistent-context choices and Live View controls remain host-only.
+
+Browserbase currently supports only a trusted-host `Unrestricted` network policy in this adapter.
+`ExactHosts` fails before allocation because Browserbase `allowedDomains` does not prove exact-host
+coverage for redirects, frames, subresources, popups and service workers. `PublicWeb` also fails
+before allocation because request interception cannot establish connection-time public-address
+containment. Neither mode silently falls back to `Unrestricted`.
+
+The adapter also exposes independent `recordings`, `replays`, and `downloads` entry points.
+Provider MP4 assembly and replay retrieval can outlive the interactive Scope; signed media URLs are
+temporary access material rather than artifact identity. Optional `capture` borrows the selected
+live page and streams bounded JPEG frames with source/receipt clocks and drop accounting. It owns
+no encoder or filesystem and does not claim website-audio capture.
+
+Host handoff pauses automation before returning temporary Live View material. Resume requires an
+explicit operator-release decision and obtains a fresh observation while retaining the mutation
+permit. Keep-alive reconnect creates a new handle generation and never replays a pending mutation.
+Persistent writers require an application-owned exclusive context lease.
+
